it has been about nine months since the  pandemic pulled clark county school  district students out of class  this morning ccsd and its biggest  teachers union announced a tentative  plan  to bring some children back to campus  hector mejia is live outside district  headquarters this this afternoon  with what they discussed hector  hey there john this is a major  development it gives us an idea of how  it's all going to play out well under  the plan ccsd schools will  reopen incrementally with the younger  students being the first returning to  campus  however there is no reopening date or  even a timeline to reopen and let's go  over some main takeaways from the  earlier meeting today  this is as you mentioned a tentative  agreement between the clark county  school district and the  clark county education association at  this point  students in grades pre-k through third  would be first to return to face-to-face  instruction  superintendent dr jesus dhara said  that's because  their team feels the younger students  need social interaction the most right  now  under the plan parents and teachers will  have the option to return  plus mandatory monthly testing for  teachers for cover 19  ppe and covet symptom screenings  contact tracing which will be helpful in  the event of an outbreak on campus  science and medical officials will be  the ones to determine  when the schools can reopen i asked the  superintendent if there's a threshold  that must be reached for them to go  ahead and make a decision to reopen  and here's what he said we're not only  looking at the covet  positivity we're also looking at our at  our mental health of our children and  our staff  we're looking at child abuse we're  looking at multiple  aspects there is no successful path  in this country to reopen these schools  under this pandemic it is really a trial  and error process  given that we have been following the  eighth largest school districts  and how they proceeded  that was ccea executive director john  villardita who believes the agreement  makes makes sense  because he said it's an incremental  approach he says it allows staff and  parents to see how  reopening on a limited basis with only  certain grades  would work at a time when the pandemic  transmission rate is rising  and again this is just a plan at this  time the clark county school  board of trustees are scheduled to go  over it and review it on january 14  and again still no date for when schools  could reopen reporting live outside ccsd  headquarters hector mejia  8 news now
 

